hment  i get laughter sometimes too but i don't  know there's tournaments for that  foosball yeah that's the one that's  that's what i do  [Music]  foosball is not just a bar room game  it's a competitive sport that's played  at a professional level by people all  around the world  it's like a hand-to-hand combat you're  standing this close you know you're  standing three feet away from your  opponent and it's almost like you're in  a fight you're battling against each  other  i come from a long line of foosball  players  i got into foosball because of my dad  he played in the the golden era the  1970s when there was a million-dollar  tour i've been playing for 20 years now  so for the first 10 to 12 years of my  career i would practice on a table at  home it would be complete repetition  over and over and over  every player in here can execute a shot  or a pass but it's a matter of  constructing a solid game plan it's like  a a game of chess on the mental side  it's it could be pretty taxing  physically by the end of the weekend  you're sore your hands are sore your  feet are sore so you have to be in  decent shape i always get a sweat band  on my arm just in case i get into a  heated match i get a  you know wipe my brow so  i go to  the world cup which is basically our  version of the olympics and i compete on  team usa  i do believe it should be in the  olympics  our only problem is the fact that  there's not a standardized foosball  table  and i'll do whatever it takes to uh for  the sport to reach that next level  bottom line is it makes me happy that  this is what i do and  yeah i love it  [Music]  oftentimes you hear people say that  they've done double dutch but most  people have never experienced what  double dutch is now it's a competitive  sport you're jumping so that you'll be  able to win  my name is kenya robinson and i'm a part  of floyd's little double dust team which  is located in north new jersey i'm 17  years old and i've been jumping double  dutch for five years  i practice with the double dust team  three times a week we compete four times  a year and it leads up to the world  competition and my team has 19 world  championship titles we're currently in  competition season and everyone is  aiming to win the trophy  joining the double dutch it gave me a  safe place it gave me a home this isn't  just jumping rope  i was born and raised in newark new  jersey and newark is a city where a lot  of violence occurs it's not always safe  to be outside a lot of shooting  happening i just never know what to  expect  growing up i didn't have the mother  relationship with my with my own mother  so i feel like coming to double dutch  has really  opened my eyes and let me know that  there is people who care about me i have  a support system whenever i need it  double dutch is where i need to be  [Music]  it takes a person with endurance to take  the person with strength it takes a  person with the positive attitude in  order to be a winner in order to be that  person who knows how to jump  in double dutch competition the most  important component of double dutch is  speed that's how fast the jumper in the  rope can jump  giving the support to the jumper is a  job that's really important to me  because growing up i didn't have that  support and i know that i want to give  the support that i never had to the  person who's in the rope to so they can  know that no matter how many mistakes  you did you can come back from it you're  still going to be a winner at the end of  the day  they have what it takes to win the  tournament  [Music]  day-to-day living i find it can be  pretty mundane and you know when i'm out  there you've just got a really simple  task which is to survive and enjoy life  my name is gavin mcclure and i'm a  cross-country paraglider  we're basically flying a modified bed  sheet and strings we don't have a motor  and we're just using thermals thermals  are kind of like the gas for a car we  get as high as we possibly can and then  we glide and if we find another thermal  we can keep going  i've flown in the himalayas i've flown  in morocco i've flown all over the alps  in europe and the canadian rockies and  we're just looking at a map in a  completely different way these days  hurricane ridge is one of the most  spectacular places  for me in the world is this beautiful  long ridge that ties right in with the  grand canyon it sits right on the edge  of zion national park  [Music]  i was doing this expedition with some of  the best pilots in the world and  right as the sun set you know the  conditions just went bang on and  we all launched into the sky and you  know paragliding can be really intense  and sometimes really scary and very  dangerous and this was like the opposite  of that it was just playful and fun and  we were doing huge wing overs and acro  and  when i'm flying over these really remote  places  i think what it gives you is a  perspective and an awe that is  impossible to get in any other way  these guys and i are people that you  know we really chase records and we  chase huge distances and made us realize  that you know it's it's not about the  records and it's not about flying huge  distances it's just about enjoying the  freedom of flight  [Music]  you
 

